      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no single \"more morally sound\" framework as each system serves distinct purposes aligned with different moral goals within modern justice systems. Retributive justice supports the moral demand for proportional accountability and societal order, while restorative justice aligns with the moral imperative of healing harm and fostering community reintegration. Many contemporary scholars argue that a hybrid approach best embodies a sophisticated moral vision, balancing the need for justice with the requirements of social reform. Ultimately, the \"better\" choice depends on whether one prioritizes assigning blame in the moment or systemic change for the future.",
