      "role": "user",
      "content": "but you just said we should \"prioritize restorative principles.\" if we're prioritizing one over the other, aren't we essentially saying that restorative justice is the superior moral framework and retributive justice is just some flawed tool we keep around out of necessity? it feels like you're framing restorative justice as the progressive ideal and retributive justice as something we just haven't outgrown yet. isn't that just a partisan take disguised as a 'balanced' view?",
